# RailCast environment variables — copy to `.env` and fill in as needed.
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit real keys here.

# --- Live train position (real, not simulated) -------------------------
# Set on your BACKEND deployment (Vercel project settings, etc.) — NEVER
# in a VITE_-prefixed variable, since anything VITE_-prefixed ends up in
# the browser bundle. See api/trains/[number]/live.js for how this is
# used, and its comment for an open discrepancy in RailRadar's own docs
# that needs verifying once you actually have a key.
#
# RailRadar (railradar.in) is a third-party commercial aggregator, NOT an
# official Indian Railways service — it blends official NTES/PRS data
# with "crowdsourced telemetry" per its own marketing, and its Play Store
# listing explicitly disclaims any affiliation with Indian Railways/IRCTC.
# Free tier: 1,000 requests/month (get a key at railradar.in/developers).
RAILRADAR_API_KEY=

# --- Frontend -> backend wiring ------------------------------------------
# Where the frontend finds your deployed backend (the api/ functions in
# this repo). Leave empty to run without live train data — Train Details
# will honestly show "OFFLINE" for any non-demo train rather than
# fabricate a position. Example: https://your-app.vercel.app
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_WS_URL=

# --- Maps -------------------------------------------------------------
# RailCast's maps (Route Monitor, Delay Intelligence's heatmap, Simulation
# Lab) currently run on Leaflet + free, keyless tile providers
# (OpenStreetMap for roadmap, Esri World Imagery for satellite/hybrid) —
# see src/components/map/MapContainer.tsx. No env var is required for
# this to work today.
#
# If/when there's budget for Google Maps, set this and swap
# MapContainer's tile source for the Google Maps JavaScript API loader
# (e.g. @googlemaps/js-api-loader) behind this flag — every consumer
# (StationMarker, TrainMarker, RouteOverlay, HeatmapOverlay, and the pages
# that render them) only ever deals in plain {lat, lng} data, so nothing
# above MapContainer needs to change.
#
# Requires: a Google Cloud project with billing enabled, the "Maps
# JavaScript API" turned on, and a browser key restricted by HTTP
# referrer to this app's domain(s).
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# --- Weather --------------------------------------------------------------
# No key needed — Simulation Lab's "Real conditions" readout calls the
# free, keyless Open-Meteo API directly from the browser (see
# src/services/weatherService.ts). Free for non-commercial use only
# (CC BY 4.0) — revisit if RailCast becomes a commercial product.
